    section: "B", questionRef: "2022 HL Q14(a)(v)",
    stem: "Section B, Question 14, part (a). Colostrum quality varies enormously between cows, so quality should be tested every time with a colostrometer or BRIX refractometer. The paper prints a Teagasc (2017) rating table for the measure of quality in milligrams of IgG in each ml of colostrum — Very good: 60 mg/ml; Good: 50 mg/ml; Poor: 30 mg/ml.",
