    stem: "Section B, Question 14, part (b). The paper prints a table (adapted from Teagasc, 2021) showing the difference in nutrient composition between colostrum, transition milk and whole milk, by milking number post calving. First milking = Colostrum, second and third = Transition Milk, fourth = Whole Milk. Total solid (%): 23.9, 17.9, 14.1, A. Fat (%): B, 5.4, 3.9, 3.8. Protein (%): C, 8.4, 5.1, 3.3.",
